  message: "Premise re-check 2026-10-25 on dev 16534a75f7 (production-CLI repros on tiny fixtures unless marked code read). CURRENT, WIDER. Fresh git repo with committed tools/my-io.yaml: `verify-claims . --claims claims.yaml --io-primitives tools/my-io.yaml` -> JSON tiers.in_repo [{git_state: committed, path: tools/my-io.yaml}], tiers.yours []; text lists it as both [CLI flag] and [in-repo, committed]. Same for an in-repo --taint-sinks file and an in-repo claims-file extra_catalogs path. No verdict change (both tiers set user_supplied, verify_claims.py:2489). Refs: cli.py:5891-5892 (I/O overlays) and :5910-5914 (taint files) build shipped=False with no origin; _resolve_io_overlay_layers (cli.py:5698-5727) has each path's origin and it is dropped at :7896; tier assignment verify_claims.py:2315; renderer dedups yours against flag paths at :2826-2828 but not in_repo at :2829-2833. OWNER RULING 2026-10-25: a claims file's extra_catalogs are NOT 'named' -- in-repo ones stay in_repo, shown with git state. Ground: ADR-0061 ruling 1's table (yours = 'a file the operator names on the command line'; in_repo = data 'the operator did not name'), ruling 4 ('Naming a file on the command line opts that file in. So --claims path/in/repo.yaml loads that claims file's extra_catalogs' -- opt-in, not re-tiering), ruling 7 ('The claims file travels with the repository'), and the INV-zosun sentence ('the repository is supplying its own criteria'). Fix: files named by --io-primitives / --taint-sinks tier yours, with git state when inside the repo (ruling 4); carry ORIGIN, not location, so opted-in .hypergumbo.toml overlays (origin in_repo_config) stay in_repo; every file listed once in text whatever its tier. P3 kept."  # 5776
